WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.300
Robert Pattinson might be running into a big
issue while preparing for The Batman.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.220
In a recent YouTube stream, Beyond the Trailer's
Grace Randolph disclosed that sources close

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.030
to the film's production are reporting that
the actor is having trouble packing on the

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.540
necessary pounds for the role.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.620
Randolph said,

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.460
"I've heard that Robert Pattinson is having
a little bit of trouble bulking up.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.660
I think it's probably impossible for him to
fully bulk up because he just has a slight

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.590
build, but I think it's hilarious they are
like, 'Maybe if we gave him a few more weeks,

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:28.620
he might bulk up'.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.300
If he hasn't bulked up by now, he's not going
to bulk up.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.940
Just accept you have skinny Batman and deal
with it."

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.080
We feel the need to point out a couple of
things here.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.579
First, Randolph's sources are anonymous, meaning
that their degree of involvement in The Batman

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.660
might be intimately involved or not involved
at all, or anything in between.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:50.540
Pattinson hasn't popped up in public at any
point super-recently, so we have no idea if

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.310
he's gotten extremely jacked for The Batman,
which is in pre-production and is thought

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.440
to be going before the cameras early next
year.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.739
Second, it's worth remembering the role that
Christian Bale played immediately prior to

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:03.520
his debut as the caped crusader in Batman
Begins.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.240
He appeared as the extremely troubled, physically
and psychologically fragile title character

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.810
in The Machinist, a role for which he lost
enough weight to pose an actual danger to

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:13.300
his health.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.740
Bale looked like a skeleton in that movie,
and just a year later, he was convincingly

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.939
playing the big, buff Dark Knight.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.560
Now, Bale and Pattinson are obviously different
people, so it's entirely possible that the

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.720
latter could be having some difficulty packing
on the muscle while the former did not.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.509
All we're saying is that the fact Pattinson
has a "slight build" doesn't mean anything

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:36.999
at all, and there's a strong possibility that
his reported struggle with bulking up is completely

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:37.580
fabricated.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.649
In fact, if you ask us, this report has the
suspicious ring of a rumor floated by parties

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:46.920
who don't think that Pattinson has what it
takes to fill out Batman's cape and cowl.

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:50.880
We'll concede that there isn't much in his
previous filmography to suggest that he has

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.820
the type of physical presence required to
portray the Caped Crusader.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.220
Still, if you're mostly familiar with the
actor from his work as sparkly vampire Edward

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.120
Cullen in the Twilight series, then you should
know that his casting was no left-field choice.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.940
"It's because you believe the lies.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.700
It's camouflage.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.700
I'm the world's most dangerous predator."

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.480
Pattinson is a serious actor, as he's demonstrated
in critically acclaimed indie films like Good

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.200
Time and High Life since his brush with franchise
fame.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.320
If you need a higher-profile, extremely recent
example of his formidable chops, look no further

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.420
than The Lighthouse.

00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:31.060
The psychological thriller from director Robert
Eggers is currently drawing critical acclaim

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:35.319
from across the board, and the stark, black-and
white period tale of two lighthouse keepers

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.440
slowly driving each other mad is largely a
two-man show.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.720
Those two men are Pattinson and Willem Dafoe,
and if the general critical consensus is to

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:48.000
be believed, the younger actor more than holds
his own opposite a man known far and wide

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.280
for giving intense, committed performances.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.440
Since we've gone this far, let's edge all
the way out onto our limb here in suggesting

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.800
that the most prominent actors to portray
Bats in the modern era Michael Keaton in Tim

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.719
Burton's films, Bale, and Ben Affleck in the
early DC Movie Universe efforts were hamstrung

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.580
by not being the most important characters
in their own movies.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.860
The Batman, as its title indicates, is shaping
up to be Pattinson's show.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:15.819
Even if the flick's director Matt Reeves builds
a tremendous rogues' gallery around him, Pattinson

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.740
has the opportunity to give us a version of
Batman that would be truly groundbreaking.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.440
We'll be able to find out for sure when The
Batman hits screens on June 25, 2021.

